    "evidence_text": "Summit County, Ohio\n\nSummit County is an urban county in the U.S. state of Ohio.\n\n Its county seat is Akron.\n\n It was named \"Summit County\" because the highest elevation on the Ohio and Erie Canal is located in the county.\n\nScapegoat Mountain\n\nScapegoat Mountain is a summit in the Scapegoat Wilderness of Lewis and Clark County, Montana, in the United States.\n\n With an elevation of 9186 ft , Scapegoat Mountain is the 443rd highest summit in the state of Montana.\n\nMcRae\u2013Helena, Georgia\n\n McRae\u2013Helena is the county seat of Telfair County.\n\nHelena is the eastern portion of Helena-West Helena, Arkansas, a city in Phillips County, Arkansas.\n\n Helena was the county seat of Phillips County until January 1, 2006, when it merged its government and city limits with neighboring West Helena.\n\nLewis and Clark County, Montana\n\nLewis and Clark County is a county located in the U.S. state of Montana.\n\n Its county seat is Helena, the state capital.\n\n The numerical designation for Lewis and Clark County (used in the issuance of the state's license plates) is 5.",
